# Orchestrator & roadmap

FactoryMate is built **milestone-by-milestone** from `docs/factorymate-roadmap.md` (M0–M14). Sub-agents implement milestones; a verifier checks them; checkboxes get ticked.

## Use the orchestrator skill when

- The user asks to "orchestrate", "delegate", "run the roadmap", "implement M3", or "develop autonomously"
- Multi-milestone work should run without the main agent implementing directly

Follow `.agents/skills/orchestrator/SKILL.md`. Do not improvise a different workflow.

## Use the roadmap directly when

- Implementing a single milestone the user already named (e.g. "do M2")
- Checking dependencies or what's next

Open `docs/factorymate-roadmap.md`, find the milestone, read tasks + DoD. Cross-check `docs/factorymate-spec.md` sections linked in `.agents/project/orchestrator/doc-index.md`.

## Milestone lifecycle

```
- [ ] not started
- [x] verified done          ← verifier only, after PASS (all task checkboxes under milestone)
- [!] failed — <reason>      ← verifier only
```

Orchestrator chat: do not edit checkboxes during execution — **verifier** sets all task checkboxes under a milestone to `[x]` / `[!]`.

## Source of truth

| Doc | Role |
| --- | --- |
| `docs/factorymate-spec.md` | Schemas, APIs, FRM, UI — implement from here |
| `docs/factorymate-roadmap.md` | Sequence and DoD only |
| `docs/frm-docs/` | FRM API reference |

Spec wins on product conflicts. Roadmap does not redefine spec.

## Frontend i18n

All `frontend/` work: follow `docs/factorymate-spec.md` §8.2 and `.cursor/rules/03-i18n.mdc` — next-intl, `messages/en.json`, no hardcoded UI strings.

Conventional commits with milestone ref: `feat(M3): implement fast-poll diff engine`. No external issue tracker in v1.
